{"availability":"available","full":"Massii-08/tls-fingerprint-scraper-demo","name":"tls-fingerprint-scraper-demo","description":"Demo: 'empty page' results on public sites are often a TLS handshake fingerprint (JA3) check before render — curl_cffi mirrors a real browser's ClientHello to read public data like a normal visitor.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-09T23:04:44Z","updated":"2026-06-09T23:49:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["browser-fingerprint","curl-cffi","http-client","ja3","public-data","python","tls-fingerprint","web-scraping"],"demo":"https://www.python.org/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T23:49:34.098Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T23:49:34.098Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T23:49:34.098Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T06:44:51.677Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T07:32:49.898Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T17:26:49.113Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-16T23:49:34.098Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Empty results behind Cloudflare are often a TLS fingerprint check before the page even renders, not a CAPTCHA.","When you read a public site with a plain Python client and get a blank body, the common assumption is \"CAPTCHA\" or \"I got blocked.\" Frequently the real cause is earlier and quieter: your client was flagged during the TLS handshake by its fingerprint (JA3 / JA4), before any HTML was served. A browser-like TLS handshake (via curlcffi with impersonate=\"chrome\") lets a legitimate client read the same public page a normal visitor sees.","This demo proves the difference safely. It reflects our own TLS fingerprint off a public echo service with two clients and compares the JA3 hashes."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Massii-08/tls-fingerprint-scraper-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6ccba9686540993b9c4295610063bfd22b6